What that means in practice (docs/DECISIONS.md DR-001, DR-003)
--------------------------------------------------------------
* The wire protocol *behaviour* is mirrored from pyeapi; the *shape of the API* is
  original TypeScript, so most modules are redesigns rather than translations.
* Every file that is a direct translation of a pyeapi function carries a short
  upstream attribution header in the source and is covered by Arista's copyright.
* Upstream documentation and test bodies were not copied verbatim. pyeapi's unit and
  system tests were ported by *behaviour* (same commands generated, same error raised)
  so the two suites stay comparable — see docs/MIGRATION.md for the symbol-by-symbol map.
* Deliberate divergences (dropped `response` key, no `Node.api('name')` autoload,
  unconditional secret redaction, named config sessions, TLS verification on by
  default, and the rest) are recorded as DR-005…DR-043 and in docs/MIGRATION.md §5.

